2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biographical notes: ==
2 CONT
2 CONT https://id.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yusuf_Al-Makassari
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Sheikh Yusuf Abul Mahasin Tajul Khalwati Al-Makasari Al-Bantani (3 July 1626 – 23 May 1699) was one of Indonesia's national heroes . [ 1 ] He was also given the title Tuanta Salamaka ri Gowa ("our savior teacher from Gowa") by h
2 CONC is supporters among the people of South Sulawesi .
2 CONT
2 CONT Sheikh Yusuf was born to Abdullah and Aminah. When he was born he was named Abadin Tadia Tjoessoep (Arabic: عابدين تاجة يوسف) or Muhammad Yusuf, [ 2 ] a name given by Sultan Alauddin (reigned from 1593 - died 15 June 1639 , the fi
2 CONC rst Muslim ruler of Gowa ), the king of Gowa , who was also a relative of Sheikh Yusuf's mother. [ 3 ]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sheikh Yusuf studied at the Cikoang Islamic Boarding School with Sheikh Sayyid Jalaluddin Bafagih (a descendant of Imam Muhammad Maula Aidid),
2 CONT
2 CONT Returning from Cikoang, Sheikh Yusuf married the daughter of the Sultan of Gowa, then at the age of 18, Sheikh Yusuf went to Banten. In Banten he became friends with Prince Surya ( Sultan Ageng Tirtayasa ), who later made him the 
2 CONC mufti of the Banten Sultanate. [ 4 ]
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1644, Syech Yusuf performed the Hajj and lived in Mecca for some time, where he studied with leading scholars in Mecca and Madina. [ 5 ] Syekh Yusuf also sought knowledge in Yemen, studying with Syekh Abdullah Muhammad bin Abd 
2 CONC Al-Baqi, and to Damascus to study with Sheikh Abu Al-Barakat Ayyub bin Ahmad bin Ayyub Al-Khalwati Al-Quraisyi. Syech Yusuf studied Islam for around 20 years in the Middle East. [ 6 ]
2 CONT
2 CONT South Africa
2 CONT
2 CONT Tomb of Sheikh Yusuf in Cape Town
2 CONT
2 CONT In South Africa, Sheikh Yusuf continued to preach, and had many followers. When he died on May 23, 1699, his followers made his death day a day of remembrance. Even Nelson Mandela , the former president of South Africa , called hi
2 CONC m 'One of the Finest Sons of Africa'.''
2 CONT ----
