1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://id.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tunibatta Wikipedia] translated
2 CONT
2 CONT Tumapa'risi' Kallonna (also spelled Tumapaqrisiq Kallonna or Tumaparisi Kallonna ) was an early karaeng or ruler of Gowa , who ruled from about 1511 to late 1546, and the first ruler to be described in detail in the Lontara Pattur
2 CONC ioloang Gowa . [ 1 ] He introduced written records and law to his kingdom, and began its expansion by conquering and establishing relations with his Makassarese neighbors . [ 2 ] He is also known for his internal reforms, includin
2 CONC g the introduction of the sabannaraq or harbormaster, the first bureaucratic position in the kingdom. [ 3 ] Under the rule of his sons and other descendants in the sixteenth century, Gowa continued its expansion and reform and eve
2 CONC ntually became a prominent power in the South Sulawesi Peninsula .
2 CONT
2 CONT Father?
2 CONT Wife: unknown
2 CONT Son: I Manggorai Daeng Mammeta (aka Karaeng Tunijallo) who married I Sambo Daeng Niasseng
