1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == I Mannuntungi aka Sultan Malikussaid (Muhammad Said)  ==
2 CONT * '''Royal name''':
2 CONT * '''Title: 15th King of Makassar, Gowa Kingdom'''
2 CONT * '''Name''': I Mannuntungi Daeng Mattola Karaeng Lakiung
2 CONT * '''Reign''': 1639 - 5th Nov 1653
2 CONT * '''Coronation''': 1639
2 CONT * '''Predecessor''': (14th King)
2 CONT * '''Successor''': (16th King) 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT * '''Title: 2nd Sultan of Gowa Sultanate'''
2 CONT * '''Name''': Sultan Malikussaid
2 CONT * '''Reign''': 1639 - 5th Nov 1653
2 CONT * '''Coronation''': 1639
2 CONT * '''Predecessor''': (1st Sultan) Alauddin 
2 CONT * '''Successor''': (3rd King)
2 CONT ----
2 CONT * '''Birth name''':
2 CONT * '''Born''': 11th Dec 1607
2 CONT * '''Died''': 5th Nov 1653 (45yo)
2 CONT * '''Burial''':
2 CONT * '''Spouse''':
2 CONT * '''Issue''': 
2 CONT * '''House''':
2 CONT * '''Father''':
2 CONT * '''Mother''':
2 CONT * '''Religion''':
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of I Sabbe To’mo Lakuntu
2 CONT Father of Hasanuddin of Gowa and Daeng Melu / Daeng Sikontu (Putri Karaeng Kasuarang)
2 CONT ----
2 CONT I Mannuntungi Dg. Mattola Krg. Lakiyung Sultan Malikussaid Raja Gowa ke-15 (1605-1653), Tumenanga ri Papang Batunna	 	
2 CONT * I Mannuntungi	
2 CONT * Daeng Mattola	
2 CONT * Karaeng Ujung, Karaeng Lakiyung	
2 CONT * Tumamenang ri Papambatuna 	
2 CONT * Raja ri Gowa ke-15 (1605-1653)
2 CONT * 15th King of Makassar Kingdom of Gowa  
2 CONT * Sultan (Muhammad Said) Malikussaid			
2 CONT * 2nd Sultan of Gowa Sultanate 
2 CONT * Reign: 1639 - 5 Nov 1653	
2 CONT * Lifetime: 11 Dec 1607 - 5 Nov 1653	
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Section 9: Tumamenang ri Papambatuna (Sultan Malikussaid)
2 CONT Tumamenang ri Papambatuna was installed as ruler because he was the child  of an equal wife.152 One hundred fifty-nine nights thence,153 at age thirty-two  he became ruler, on the day of Araba, the twelfth of the month of Safar, t
2 CONC he  fifteenth of the Christian month of June. He became ruler on Tuesday the  eighteenth, the twenty-first of the Christian month.154 
2 CONT He informed Tumammaliang ri Timoroq, the tumailalang, the anaq karaeng,  the gallarrang,155 ‘If I am to be karaeng, together with Tumamenappa ri Bontobiraeng [Karaeng Pattingalloang] I will rule, for he guides all the people.’ 	Th
2 CONC e name of this karaeng, may I not be cursed, was I Mannuntung. His  royal name was I Daeng Mattola. His karaeng-title before he ruled was  Karaeng Ujung. It was later changed to Karaeng Lakiung. 
2 CONT
2 CONT When he was young he was promised in marriage to a child of the  Arumpone [25v] named I Lapalang. [The Arumpone] was called Matinroa  ri Talloq. His fiancee died and he was promised in marriage to a child of  Tumammaliang ri Timor
2 CONC oq named I Ranga. Her royal name was I Daeng  Mateqne. Her karaeng-title was Karaeng ri Tangallaq. She was a child of  Karaeng Tumammaliang ri Timoroq by a child of Karaeng ri Barombong.  Her mother’s personal name was I Bijawi.15
2 CONC 6 Her royal name was I Daeng  Kaling. Upon reaching puberty, he married her while she was still small. They  divorced. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He then married a child of Karaeng Matoaya named I Baine. Her royal  name was I Kare Maqnassa. She was named Daenta ri Pattingalloang. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He then married one from Laikang living in Pattoppakang named I Saqbe.  Her royal name was I Loqmoq Kontu. She had two children. A daughter  named I Patima, her Makassarese name was I Saniq. Her royal name was I  Daeng Nisakking. 
2 CONC Her karaeng-title was Karaeng Bontojeqneq. A son named  Muhammad Bakir, his Makassarese name was I Mallombasi. His royal name  was I Daeng Mattawang. His karaeng-title before he ruled was Karaeng 
2 CONT Bontomangape. These were all his children before he became ruler.
2 CONT
2 CONT He then divorced Daenta ri Pattingalloang. He married Karaeng ri  Tangallaq. He married and then became ruler. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Upon ruling he married  again a friend of one from Tallampuang, one from Binamuq named I Bissu.  Her royal name was I Kare Jannang. She had one daughter named I Rabia.  Her Makassarese name was I Sungguminasa. Her royal name was I
2 CONC  Daeng  Nisanga. Her karaeng-title was Karaeng Sanggiringang. After two years he  and Karaeng ri Tangallaq divorced.
2 CONT
2 CONT He then married again to a first cousin, one from Sanrabone named I  Ranga. Her royal name was I Daeng Marannu. They had no children. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Then he married a granddaughter of Karaeng Matoaya, a child of Daenta  ri Mangeppeq by Karaeng ri Cenrana named I Mallewai. Her royal name was  I Daeng Maqnassa.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married. I Ralle was her Makassarese name. Her royal name was I  Daeng Paikaq. She had one daughter named I Manneratu. Her royal name  was I Daeng Niasseng. Her karaeng-title was Karaeng ri Bontomateqne. It was  later changed t
2 CONC o Karaeng ri Lakiung. Her Javanese name was I Sapuru.157  Another, only a slave, gave birth to one named I Asseng. [I Asseng’s]  mother was I Yata. [I Asseng’s] royal name was I Loqmoq Singaraq. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Another was a son. A mere household woman gave birth to him. [24r] Named I Tanriwalu, his Arabic name158 was I Sepulo. His Makassarese name was I Atatojeng. His royal name was I Kare Tulolo. His karaeng-title was  Karaeng Bontomaj
2 CONC annang.159 
2 CONT This karaeng never faced epidemics, never faced fierce wars, never faced 
2 CONT great famines. 
2 CONT
2 CONT It was this karaeng who befriended the governor in Manila, the viceroy  in Goa, the president in Coromandel, the Mir Jumla in Machhilipatnam, the  ruler of the English, the ruler of the Portuguese, the ruler of the Spanish.  Befri
2 CONC ending the mufti in Mekka, he was the karaeng who first was  titled [Sultan] by Mekka. Named Muhammad Said, his name indeed was  Malikussaid. 
2 CONT
2 CONT This karaeng was praised among the karaeng as a proficient reciter, was  praised as a man respectful toward the elders, was praised as governing  kindly with his subjects. 
2 CONT
2 CONT This karaeng was adept at having visions, adept at honouring others,  adept at repaying generosity. He was loved by the people, though the anaq  karaeng and the tumailalang loved Tumamenang ri Gaukanna more.
2 CONT
2 CONT This karaeng was skilled at writing Arabic, very good at writing Makassarese.160 
