1 NAME Raja Talaga III - Darmasuci II
1 SEX M
1 OCCU King
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Raja Talaga abt 1388 - 1420.
2 CONT
2 CONT =============================================Note on 6 Nov 2010/em:
2 CONT
2 CONT Link to his profile in Joyce Tree:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.geni.com/people/Sunan-Talaga-Manggung/6000000003011145612
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Sunan Talaga Manggung, also known as Prabu Darma Suci II, was well known and well loved until now, for his sense of wisdom and justice. His attention to a Hinduism was high. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He paid attention to agricultural developments, irrigations, traditional handicrafts and art, including folk art. His good relations and diplomacy with neighboring kingdoms, or faraway kingdoms were also known. He had relations to
2 CONC  Majapahit Kingdom, Pajajaran Kingdom, Cirebon Kingdom and also Sriwijaya Kingdom.
2 CONT
2 CONT His reign was known as the time where Talaga Kingdom was glorious and social conditions were stable and calm. Many people coming from other places would go and settle in Talaga because of this.
2 CONT
2 CONT He had two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Raden Panglurah - 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Ratu Simbarkencana 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was murdered by her own son in law, Palembang Gunung's man, named Centangbarang. Palembang Gunung  took Sunan Talaga Manggung's reign but did not reign long. He was married to Queen Simbarkencana. 
2 CONT
2 CONT When Queen Simbarkencana found out what happened to her father, she killed Palembang Gunung with the instruction of  hulubalang Citrasinga (King's Advisor) using a hair pin (tusuk konde) while he was sleeping. After the death of P
2 CONC alembang Gunung, the Queen took the reign, and then remarried - this time to a descendant of Panjalu - named Raden Kusumalaya Ajar Kutamanggu and had 8 children. One of the most known was her first son, Sunan Parung.
2 CONT
2 CONT Stories:
2 CONT
2 CONT Prabu Darmasuci II (Prabu Talagamanggung) lived in Talaga in his castle located in Sangiang. Situ Sangiang is the castle location. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a both skilled and had shakti and was bullet proof. He had a talisman named "cis", that had a form of a small spear (sekin). As the story goes, he was born without a navel. According the legend, Prabu Talagamanggung can onl
2 CONC y be wounded by his own talisman, his CIS.
2 CONT
2 CONT When he was murdered by Centangbarang, who worked for his 'son in law'. The son in law wanted to take over the reign. So it was told that he took 'cis' from Sunan Talaga Manggung - and then used it to kill the King. He died and hi
2 CONC s ashes was scattered in Situ Sangiang. 
2 CONT
2 CONT And Talagamanggung's daughter, Simbarkencana killed her own husband upon finding out that her father was murdered under the instruction of no other than her own husband. She took over the reign and squashed the underground movemen
2 CONC t started by her husband. 
